{"pk": "1287", "sid": "PKDB00799", "name": "Swanson1984", "licence": "open", "access": "public", "date": "2024-04-24", "group_count": 3, "individual_count": 0, "intervention_count": 1, "output_count": 86, "output_calculated_count": 12, "subset_count": 14, "timecourse_count": 14, "scatter_count": 0, "reference": {"pk": 1295, "study": {"sid": "PKDB00799", "name": "Swanson1984"}, "pmid": "6097665", "sid": "6097665", "name": "Swanson1984", "doi": null, "title": "Influence of food on the bioavailability of enalapril.", "abstract": "In a randomized, two-period crossover study in 12 normal volunteers, serum and urine concentrations of the angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor enalapril and its active metabolite enalaprilat were determined following administration of a single 40-mg tablet of enalapril maleate administered both in the fasting state and with a standard breakfast. A 7-d interval separated the two treatment periods. Area under the serum concentration-time curves for enalaprilat and urinary recoveries for enalaprilat and total drug did not differ significantly between the fed and fasted conditions. The mean observed maximum serum concentration of enalaprilat was slightly higher for the fasting treatment, but the time to peak concentration was almost identical for the two treatments. Enalapril maleate is unlike the prototype angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor captopril in that a standard meal does not appear to influence absorption of this new drug.", "journal": "Journal of pharmaceutical sciences", "date": "1985-02-27", "authors": [{"pk": 7466, "first_name": "B N", "last_name": "Swanson"}, {"pk": 7467, "first_name": "P H", "last_name": "Vlasses"}, {"pk": 7468, "first_name": "R K", "last_name": "Ferguson"}, {"pk": 7469, "first_name": "P A", "last_name": "Bergquist"}, {"pk": 7470, "first_name": "A E", "last_name": "Till"}, {"pk": 7471, "first_name": "J D", "last_name": "Irvin"}, {"pk": 7472, "first_name": "K", "last_name": "Harris"}]}, "reference_date": "1985-02-27", "creator": {"username": "shubhankarpalwankar", "first_name": "Shubhankar", "last_name": "Palwankar"}, "curators": [{"rating": 3.0, "username": "shubhankarpalwankar", "first_name": "Shubhankar", "last_name": "Palwankar"}, {"rating": 0.0, "username": "mkoenig", "first_name": "Matthias", "last_name": "K\u00f6nig"}], "collaborators": [], "comments": [], "descriptions": [{"pk": 4970, "text": "Twelve healthy, normotensive male subjects (age, 23-37 years)"}, {"pk": 4971, "text": "good health; diastolic blood pressure (<=90 mm Hg)"}, {"pk": 4972, "text": "open, randomized, two-way crossover study"}, {"pk": 4973, "text": "enalapril maleate (40 mg) was administered as a single dose"}, {"pk": 4974, "text": "Subjects fasted from midnight of the previous night. On the first day of each treatment period, subjects received doses of enalapril maleate either in a fasting state or immediately after a standard prescribed breakfast"}, {"pk": 4975, "text": "Blood was drawn at 0, I, 2,3.4,6,8, 12, 16,24,36,48,60, and 72 h"}, {"pk": 4976, "text": "Urine was collected at -1-0,0-2,2-4,4-6,6-8,8-12,12-24,24-36,36-48,48-72,72-96 and 96-120 h"}], "files": [{"pk": 15692, "name": "data/Swanson1984_Fig1.png", "file": "/media/data/Swanson1984_Fig1.png"}, {"pk": 15697, "name": "data/.Swanson1984_Fig1.tsv", "file": "/media/data/.Swanson1984_Fig1.tsv"}, {"pk": 15690, "name": "data/Swanson1984_Fig2.png", "file": "/media/data/Swanson1984_Fig2.png"}, {"pk": 15695, "name": "data/.Swanson1984_Fig2.tsv", "file": "/media/data/.Swanson1984_Fig2.tsv"}, {"pk": 15693, "name": "data/Swanson1984_Fig3.png", "file": "/media/data/Swanson1984_Fig3.png"}, {"pk": 15696, "name": "data/.Swanson1984_Fig3.tsv", "file": "/media/data/.Swanson1984_Fig3.tsv"}, {"pk": 15686, "name": "data/Swanson1984.pdf", "file": "/media/data/Swanson1984.pdf"}, {"pk": 15689, "name": "data/.Swanson1984_Tab1B.tsv", "file": "/media/data/.Swanson1984_Tab1B.tsv"}, {"pk": 15691, "name": "data/Swanson1984_Tab1.png", "file": "/media/data/Sw